"""Freeze the six-case exploratory extension; the core GDPR-30 dataset is unchanged."""
import hashlib,json
from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
PKG=P.parents[1]
if (P/'cases.json').exists():raise FileExistsError('Frozen study exists; use a fresh directory')
def write(name,data):
 (P/name).write_text(json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
common={'party_role':'controller','supervisory_authority_decision_on_communication':'no_decision'}
def facts(**kw):return dict(common,**kw)
base=facts(breach_unlikely_to_result_in_risk=False,breach_likely_to_result_in_high_risk=True,appropriate_protection_measures_applied_to_affected_data=False,subsequent_measures_ensure_high_risk_no_longer_likely=False,communication_would_involve_disproportionate_effort=False)
cases=[
{'id':'E01','title':'Encrypted medical backup and an unverified key exposure','scenario':'A private rehabilitation company discovers a stolen backup containing identifiable psychiatric findings. The backup uses strong encryption. Primary records remain available. An administrator laptop holding access credentials to the separate key vault was also stolen. Whether those credentials can unlock the vault, whether a second factor was required, and whether keys were accessed are not yet known. Key-vault logs will not be available until tomorrow. The incident team has not completed its risk assessment. Patients are individually reachable. No supervisory-authority decision on communication exists.', 'questions':[{'id':'q1','prompt':'Can you determine now whether individual notification is legally required? State what is known and what must be established; do not assume that encryption or theft alone settles it.'},{'id':'q2','prompt':'May the company defer the whole breach-risk assessment and all response work until the key audit arrives tomorrow? Give the immediate priorities.'}], 'demo_requests':[{'id':'E01.main','facts':facts(communication_would_involve_disproportionate_effort=False),'limits':'Risk and effective unintelligibility are unknown and omitted. The book cannot determine key compromise or decide response sequencing.'}]},
{'id':'E02','title':'Friday anomaly, Monday confirmation, different reporting roles','scenario':'An IT processor hosts a private hospital portal. On Friday at 18:00, monitoring shows failed login attempts, but no evidence then establishes unauthorised access, loss or disclosure. The processor starts a reasonable investigation immediately. On Monday at 18:00 it confirms that readable named diagnoses were downloaded; this is the first evidence providing reasonable certainty of a personal data breach. It informs the hospital controller at 18:20. The hospital had no earlier information about the incident. It is now Monday 18:30. Blackmail and stigma are plausible, downloaded copies cannot be recalled, and patients are reachable. No authority decision on communication exists.', 'questions':[{'id':'q1','prompt':'Did the hospital controller necessarily miss its Article 33 deadline because 72 hours have passed since Friday? Distinguish suspicion, established awareness and the processor/controller duties.'},{'id':'q2','prompt':'Must the controller notify the supervisory authority now, or may it wait for a complete forensic report? Explain the role of without undue delay and phased information.'}], 'demo_requests':[{'id':'E02.main','facts':base,'limits':'Breach duties only. Friday/Monday awareness times, role-specific timing and adequacy of investigation are not represented in this book.'}]},
{'id':'E03','title':'Deleted public health-data link without download logs','scenario':'A private clinic confirms that named HIV treatment reports were publicly readable through an indexed link for 18 hours. Access logs were never enabled, so it cannot prove or disprove downloads. It removes the link. The leaked data were plaintext; people are identifiable and individually reachable. The incident team reasonably assesses likely high risk of serious stigma from the confirmed exposure. No evidence shows that all possible copies have been recalled or that high risk has ceased. There is no supervisory-authority decision on communication.', 'questions':[{'id':'q1','prompt':'Is individual communication required even though no completed download can be proved? Explain the threshold and information to communicate.'},{'id':'q2','prompt':'Does deleting the public link establish the subsequent-measures exception under Article 34(3)(b) on these facts? Explain what the deletion does and does not establish.'}], 'demo_requests':[{'id':'E03.main','facts':base,'limits':'High risk is a stated case assessment, not derived by the engine. The engine does not analyse access logs or prove recall.'}]},
{'id':'E04','title':'Mixed contactability across 100,000 affected people','scenario':'A service network confirms external download of plaintext health complaints linked to 100,000 people, with a documented likely high risk of blackmail. The exposure has been closed but copied data remain outside its control. Group A contains 70,000 people with verified contact details; individual communication is feasible and proportionate. For group B, 30,000 people, documented reasonable attempts establish that individual contact would involve disproportionate effort. Marketing proposes one banner behind a login for everyone. Only 20% of group B used the portal in the last year; there is no evidence that this banner informs group B equally effectively, and no other substitute channels have yet been evaluated. No authority decision on communication exists.', 'questions':[{'id':'q1','prompt':'May the network replace individual communication to group A with the proposed banner merely because group B is difficult to contact? Explain the group-specific duties.'},{'id':'q2','prompt':'Has the network established that the proposed banner alone fulfils its communication obligation to group B? Distinguish permission to use a substitute from proof that this substitute is sufficient.'}], 'demo_requests':[{'id':'E04.A','facts':base,'limits':'Represents group A only.'},{'id':'E04.B','facts':dict(base,communication_would_involve_disproportionate_effort=True),'limits':'Represents disproportionate effort for group B. The input schema has no field for equal effectiveness of this specific banner. A public-communication output is not a certification of the banner.'}]},
{'id':'E05','title':'Austrian hospital with unclear public mandate','scenario':'A hospital operator established in Austria processes central health records for 120,000 patients annually as an indispensable part of clinical treatment. It is a GmbH. The ownership structure, public-law status, and whether it acts under a statutory public mandate have not been established. Do not infer private or public-body status from GmbH alone. A potential GDPR fine is under consideration, but neither its final amount nor the legal applicability of the Austrian public-body exemption has been determined.', 'questions':[{'id':'q1','prompt':'Must this operator designate a DPO under Article 37(1)(c), despite the unresolved public/private classification? Explain the relevant facts and next steps.'},{'id':'q2','prompt':'Can you determine from these facts whether Austria\'s DSG section 30(5) excludes GDPR fines for this operator? Identify the missing legal and factual checks.'}], 'demo_requests':[]},
{'id':'E06','title':'Contradictory risk flags and verified blackmail','scenario':'A clinic confirms that identifiable psychiatric notes were downloaded in plaintext and published by an attacker. Several named patients have received credible blackmail messages quoting those notes. Patients are individually reachable. No subsequent measure removes this danger. There is no authority decision on communication. A copied incident form nevertheless marks BOTH "unlikely to result in a risk" and "likely to result in a high risk" as true. These flags describe the same incident, people, time and harms; the first flag is an unreasoned checkbox, not an additional factual finding.', 'questions':[{'id':'q1','prompt':'Are the two input flags coherent, and may a no-notification result based on the low-risk checkbox be accepted? Explain how the input conflict should be handled.'},{'id':'q2','prompt':'On the independently established narrative facts, must the controller communicate to the affected people now? Explain whether correcting the form may delay the response.'}], 'demo_requests':[{'id':'E06.conflict','facts':dict(base,breach_unlikely_to_result_in_risk=True),'limits':'Deliberately conflicting risk inputs are submitted unchanged as a robustness test. Do not prefer a returned result to established facts solely because it came from a rule engine.'}]}
]
# All conditions receive this identical factual encoding, including explicit omissions/limitations.
write('cases.json',cases)
gold={
'E01.q1':(['unknown','conditional'],['Do not infer safe keys or mandatory individual communication from the incomplete facts alone','Identify key accessibility and risk assessment as unresolved','Urgently reassess rather than treating uncertainty as exemption']),
'E01.q2':(['no'],['Start assessment and containment now','Investigate/revoke credentials or secure keys without waiting','Apply notification thresholds promptly, document and update']),
'E02.q1':(['no'],['Friday suspicion does not establish controller awareness','Distinguish processor awareness Monday18:00 and controller Monday18:20','Processor without-undue-delay and controller separate clock; no automatic72h waiting entitlement']),
'E02.q2':(['yes'],['Risk makes authority notification required','Without undue delay, not a full72h waiting allowance','Initial available information then phased updates; document']),
'E03.q1':(['yes'],['Confirmed exposure and stipulated high risk suffice without proved download','Reject automatic exemption for no logs/no proof','Prompt plain-language communication with contact/consequences/measures']),
'E03.q2':(['no'],['Deletion closes future access','No evidence high risk from copies no longer likely','Document and reassess rather than assuming recall']),
'E04.q1':(['no'],['GroupA remains directly reachable/proportionate','Do not extend groupB exception to all','Prompt direct communication to A']),
'E04.q2':(['no'],['Disproportionate effort permits substitute but does not eliminate communication','Equal effectiveness of this banner not established','Develop/evidence effective additional channels; do not assume20percent historical use equals current actual reach']),
'E05.q1':(['yes'],['Health data specialcategory','Core and large-scale120k trigger irrespective publicprivate','Designate/involve qualified DPO with contacts and independence']),
'E05.q2':(['unknown','conditional'],['GmbH alone does not settle exemption','Examine statutory mandate and actual legal/public-body qualification','No unconditional exemption or automatic fine; Austrian/EU legal assessment needed']),
'E06.q1':(['no'],['Sameincident flags contradictory','Reject unreasoned lowrisk conclusion and correct/escalate inputs','Do not erase evidentiary facts or blindly follow engine']),
'E06.q2':(['yes'],['Verified plaintextpsychiatric disclosure and blackmail establish high risk','No stated exception applies','Communicate promptly; fixing form must not delay'])}
write('gold.provisional.json',{'status':'provisional','independent_review':'pending','frozen_before_runs':True,'answers':{q:{'accepted_decisions':d,'critical_points':p} for q,(d,p) in gold.items()}})
write('freeze.json',{n:hashlib.sha256((P/n).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for n in ['cases.json','gold.provisional.json']})
(P/'PROTOCOL.md').write_text('''# Six-case exploratory paired pilot — protocol frozen before inference

This separate extension leaves GDPR-30 and its 70 original questions unchanged. Six synthetic boundary cases, two questions each. Four requested models: gpt-6.1-sol, gpt-6-astra, claude-opus-5-5, claude-sonnet-5-5. Three parallel conditions: law; law+RIS decisions; law+Mike demo output (not cumulative with RIS). One fresh batch containing all six cases per model/condition: 12 calls, 72 case-condition records, 144 question answers if all succeed. No retries of successful inference, no fallback substitution. Missing runs remain missing.

All conditions receive identical case narratives, normalized facts, omission notes and coverage limitations. Common law includes relevant full GDPR articles plus Austrian DSG sections5/30 (retrieved via RIS but statutory text is common to all). RIS treatment adds two complete DSB decisions previously retrieved through RIS MCP. Mike treatment adds only actually returned exploratory outputs for the frozen facts. No reviewed gold, evaluator notes or other models' answers enter prompts. No held-out bypass. Unknown fields are omitted; E06 deliberately sends conflicting flags. No engine support is invented for E05 or time-computation questions.

The primary comparison is within-model answer quality: Mike minus law on identical questions; RIS minus law is a secondary comparison. Decision-label agreement alone is insufficient. Assistant assessment: 0 = materially wrong/unsafe conclusion or reasoning, 1 = correct core conclusion but material critical-point omission, 2 = correct conclusion and all three critical points substantively addressed. A materially correct qualified answer may receive2 despite alternate label wording; label agreement is reported separately. Cite excerpt/reason for every deduction. Report improved/unchanged/worse questions and case-level summed score changes. The rater is the same assistant preparing the study, not an independent lawyer; blind IDs are a review aid, not independent blinded validation. Gold is provisional.

H0: no within-model quality improvement from the demo supplement. H1: higher quality with the demo supplement. Six cases are clusters; questions/models are not independent samples. Report a descriptive effect and exact paired sign test on nonzero case-level deltas (averaged across available paired models), exploratory only, no significance-based superiority claim, no power claim. Report missing/held-out/unsupported coverage alongside scores. A ceiling result cannot establish equivalence. Underlying CLI harnesses differ by provider, so cross-provider rankings are exploratory. Medium effort is not equal compute across providers. Costs from subscription routes are not invoices; record emitted usage and any provider cost estimate separately.

Supplied-fact retrieval is intentional: this tests answer generation with evidence, not autonomous tool selection or fact extraction. Models may reject tool outputs contradicted by facts/law. New input interpretations and source ordering remain possible confounds. No external human review, immutable backend guarantee, full production-API test or complete GDPR-Prolog validation is claimed.
''')
print('Prepared six cases, twelve questions and provisional rubric.')
